+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory Is In Scope; Free-Text Veterinarian Search Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 barred searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. It was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so its provenance stayed open.
+
+On 2026-08-25 the owner asked for the veterinarian directory to be narrowable to one specialty, on both the page and the machine-readable surface. Read whole, NG-9 would bar that request. Read as written, it bars search — typing free text and getting ranked or prefix-matched entities back. That is a different capability from narrowing a published list to a value it already prints in every row.
+
+The boundary had to settle which reading governs before the request could proceed.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-9 whole and decline the request.** Rejected: it would decline a capability that adds no new search surface, on the strength of a row derived from absence.
+2. **Withdraw NG-9 entirely.** Rejected: the rationale for declining free-text search across pets, visits, and veterinarians still holds. Owner search demonstrates the pattern once.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 bars free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. Narrowing a list to one attribute that the list already shows is not search, and stays in scope.
+
+The veterinarian directory is the first list to take a narrowing, by specialty. A later request to narrow another list by an attribute it already shows falls inside the narrowed row and needs no further decision. A request for free-text search over any entity still needs an explicit owner decision recorded at intake.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- REQ-VET-001 gains the narrowing on the page surface, and the fresh REQ-VET-003 carries it on the machine-readable surface.
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation. Every other undecided row remains part of it.
+- The directory gains no page control in this decision. Whether it should is recorded as an open question, not as declined scope.
+- Free-text veterinarian search remains out of scope and is now stated as such, rather than implied by a broader row.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+## References
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble that names it decided.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-001) — the requirements the narrowing lands in.
+- [Case-Insensitive Specialty Matching Lives in the Query](2026-08-25-case-insensitive-specialty-matching.md) — how the narrowing this decision admits is matched.
